<div class="mb-4" data-controller="prompt-preprocessing">
  <div class="form-check form-switch">
    <%= form.check_box :prompt_preprocessing_enabled, class: 'form-check-input', role: 'switch',
                       aria: { controls: 'prompt_preprocessing_settings', expanded: workflow.prompt_preprocessing_enabled? },
                       data: { prompt_preprocessing_target: 'toggle', action: 'prompt-preprocessing#update' } %>
    <%= form.label :prompt_preprocessing_enabled, 'Enable prompt preprocessing', class: 'form-check-label' %>
  </div>
  <%= tag.div id: 'prompt_preprocessing_settings', class: 'mt-3',
              hidden: !workflow.prompt_preprocessing_enabled?, data: { prompt_preprocessing_target: 'settings' } do %>
    <p class="text-13 text-secondary mb-2">
      Before generating, Comfier sends the user's prompt (and lyrics, if provided) to the
      <strong>chat</strong> model through LiteLLM, using the system prompt below.
      Its response replaces <code>{{prompt}}</code> in this workflow and is passed to the generation model.
      For an image workflow, that response becomes the image prompt.
    </p>
    <p class="text-12 text-secondary mb-2">
      This adds a text-generation step and some waiting time. The user's original prompt is kept;
      the rewritten prompt is shown on the result page. If preprocessing fails, generation stops with an error.
    </p>
    <% if LiteLlm::Client.url.blank? %>
      <div class="status-panel status-attention text-13 mb-2">
        LiteLLM is not configured. Set LITELLM_URL before using preprocessing; the gateway must provide a chat model.
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <%= form.label :prompt_preprocessing_system_prompt, 'Preprocessing system prompt', class: 'form-label' %>
    <%= form.text_area :prompt_preprocessing_system_prompt, rows: 7,
                      value: workflow.prompt_preprocessing_system_prompt || PromptPreprocessor::DEFAULT_SYSTEM_PROMPT,
                      class: 'form-control form-control-sm', required: workflow.prompt_preprocessing_enabled?,
                      data: { prompt_preprocessing_target: 'prompt' },
                      placeholder: 'Describe how chat should rewrite the user’s input. Ask it to return only the finished prompt.' %>
    <div class="form-text text-12">
      The starting instructions are for visual artwork. Edit them for this workflow and ask chat to return only
      the prompt the generation model should receive. This workflow must contain <code>{{prompt}}</code>.
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
